{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence","id":987981,"title":"Death influence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-15T16:06:23-07:00","id":987981,"title":"Death influence","content":"Hey guys, my troup got some trouble to use death influence , i was thinking to se death arcanum from mage as guide , but i whats a uratha can really do with death influence ar four?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T16:25:30-07:00","id":987993,"title":"","content":"Probably cause straight necrotic damage with Create Death. With the first three I'd imagine possibly some wounds or illnesses becoming profoundly more nasty, like getting the worst of the tilt effects. You could empower or weaken ghosts.<br /> <br /> I think using Manipulation you could 'stave off' an otherwise immediate Death.<br /> <br /> If you do use the Death Arcanum, I'd suggest keeping it focused to Death-specific actions, as the Arcanum really encompasses a lot more than a spirit of death might. I think, at least. I haven't much thought of it but I suppose Influence Death might have similar purview. Not entirely, but for the most part. Would be interesting to see other views on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T13:03:14-07:00","id":988349,"title":"","content":"I would say Strengthen Death could speed up entropic processes, causing withering or decaying things to break down at an accelerated rate, maybe aging subjects rapidly or shortening their lifespans; basically anything the artifact from the Moon Window story seed in GMC could do. Manipulate Death is kind of tricky, but I agree with nofather you could probably use it to stave off death, slowing the same processes Strengthen Death accelerates. With Control Death I reckon you'd be able to alter those entropic effects horizontally - maybe change what a subject is dying from, or alter the way in which matter is breaking down. Create Death seems pretty straightforward, it kills things. Although since Create is always temporary without Influence 5, anything you killed with it would come back eventually. Once you get to Mass Create Death, you can kill lots of subjects for a short time, or a single subject permanently. All this is, of course, in addition to the effects all Influences can have on like-aligned Manifestation Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:04:43-07:00","id":988487,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure anything you killed with Create Death would stay dead. In Mage parlance, it's a lasting effect.<br /> <br /> For example stuff you burn with Create Fire stays burned. Same principle applies here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:17:09-07:00","id":988493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=988487#post988487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure anything you killed with Create Death would stay dead. In Mage parlance, it's a lasting effect.<br /> <br /> For example stuff you burn with Create Fire stays burned. Same principle applies here.</div> </div> </div> </div>With create fire, the burns are a result of the fire not the fire itself. The fire itself disappears after the abilities duration.<br /> <br /> So with create death, things that are a result of the death (like idk, a loved one's panic attack or animals eating parts of the body while the person is dead) will last but the death itself disappears after the abilities duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:39:45-07:00","id":988504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=988493#post988493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with create death, things that are a result of the death will last ... after the abilities duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering they won't be breathing while it lasts, this conveniently includes &quot;being dead&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:49:13-07:00","id":988514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=988504#post988504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering they won't be breathing while it lasts, this conveniently includes &quot;being dead&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't need to breathe while dead in this way since their brain is already dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T17:06:11-07:00","id":988525,"title":"","content":"Alright, what about the blood clots that'll probably form if your heart just stops for a few minutes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:07:50-07:00","id":988543,"title":"","content":"For Create Death doing straight damage I was referring to necrosis, the death of living cells, not just a feign death situation.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/marveldatabase/images/8/87/Laurie_Collins_%26_Kevin_Ford_(Earth-616).jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> If it's doing Lethal, it's not a matter of 'Put some ice on it and rest for an hour.'<br /> <br /> You can do a search for necrotizing if you want more graphic images.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:15:27-07:00","id":988546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=988525#post988525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, what about the blood clots that'll probably form if your heart just stops for a few minutes?</div> </div> </div> </div>The persons blood would not clot in areas that lack damage, as the blood would not come in contact with collagen. So that isn't an issue either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:01:27-07:00","id":988578,"title":"","content":"So many good ideas, a irraka from house of death wants upgrade damage on enemies with strenghten death , this is really possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:06:03-07:00","id":988581,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, increasing damage is definitely possible. Just like Influence can be used to enhance health, structure, or whatever. If its tied to the concept it can be Strengthened, Manipulated, Controlled, or Created to do what you want in that purview. Sadly, its pretty esoteric and thematic rather than being hardcoded mechanically. So people have to basically come up with what they want to be legal at their own table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T00:02:58-07:00","id":988721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=988578#post988578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So many good ideas, a irraka from house of death wants upgrade damage on enemies with strenghten death , this is really possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say it depends on the nature of the attack. Biting or clawing? Probably not. Shooting someone with a gun? Again, I'd say no. Stabbing them with a Fetish weapon with a death spirit bound to it? Absolutely. Using a Rite on an effigy of your prey to inflict them with necrosis? You'd better believe it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T01:42:23-07:00","id":988738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=988546#post988546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The persons blood would not clot in areas that lack damage, as the blood would not come in contact with collagen. So that isn't an issue either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood can clot internally. Have you never heard of deep vein thrombosis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T05:51:11-07:00","id":988811,"title":"","content":"I would feel quite content, for my games, ruling that someone slain by Create Death would remain thoroughly dead when the supernatural effect lifted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T05:38:23-07:00","id":989303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=988811#post988811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would feel quite content, for my games, ruling that someone slain by Create Death would remain thoroughly dead when the supernatural effect lifted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah i feel the same, but i would Make a withstand vigor rule like mage to avoid a insta kill move, even if my players could use it once for story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T05:56:13-07:00","id":989305,"title":"","content":"Spells that do direct damage via Fraying aren't Withstood. The idea is the Stamina is already factored in, because of their Health. And that's just using Mage rules.<br /> <br /> By ephemeral rules, with Influence, you are creating death. I don't see why there is a need to think up roadblocks for death having the potential to do damage and possibly kill people. You could do the same with Create Fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-18-2016, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T06:13:30-07:00","id":989313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=989305#post989305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spells that do direct damage via Fraying aren't Withstood. The idea is the Stamina is already factored in, because of their Health. And that's just using Mage rules.<br /> <br /> By ephemeral rules, with Influence, you are creating death. I don't see why there is a need to think up roadblocks for death having the potential to do damage and possibly kill people. You could do the same with Create Fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if ephemeral was intended to work like that so be it, lodge of Death and the eater of deads will be fearsome\ud83d\ude00,some players are arguing if their can create a portal t\u00f4 underworld with influence 4, but I think ir Will work better as a ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T06:16:40-07:00","id":989314,"title":"","content":"Opening an Avernian Gate is a separate ability powerful death-aspected spirits can have, so yeah, I don't think the influence covers it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T06:27:40-07:00","id":989320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=989313#post989313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if ephemeral was intended to work like that so be it, lodge of Death and the eater of deads will be fearsome</div> </div> </div> </div>My character bit someone for six Aggravated damage. That's with two Strength and 1 Brawl in human form. Werewolves are fearsome, and should be.<br /> <br /> Presuming you're talking about Lodge Sorcery, there is a prerequisite of a five Dot Merit and it still relies on fueling the power with 4 Essence and relying on a Presence + Wits roll. Werewolves can do considerably more with much less of an investment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> some players are arguing if their can create a portal t\u00f4 underworld with influence 4, but I think ir Will work better as a ritual. </div> </div> </div>I think that requires a rite. In first edition, at least, it was a four Dot Ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-18-2016, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T07:03:41-07:00","id":989327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=989320#post989320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My character bit someone for six Aggravated damage. That's with two Strength and 1 Brawl in human form. Werewolves are fearsome, and should be.<br /> <br /> Presuming you're talking about Lodge Sorcery, there is a prerequisite of a five Dot Merit and it still relies on fueling the power with 4 Essence and relying on a Presence + Wits roll. Werewolves can do considerably more with much less of an investment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think that requires a rite. In first edition, at least, it was a four Dot Ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>LOL<br /> <br /> First, how you give 6 agravated with that pool?<br /> <br /> inded fearsome, my only problem is a concept of &quot;fairness&quot; on COD creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T07:18:20-07:00","id":989338,"title":"","content":"Urshul gave +2 to Strength, Willpower +3 to diceroll. Eating for flesh does Aggravated.<br /> <br /> I understand. If you're doing a mixed game you might tone it down, but really it's still a big cost for one action. Four Essence is a lot, and if they were to get the Tongue of Flame Gift they would be able to do it with a larger dicepool once they had the Purity for it. And that's without tying themselves to a lodge totem with a nasty ban.<br /> <br /> Werewolves face foes that are very powerful and can do a lot of damage very easily. The same character's first encounter with a Rank 2 spirit had the creature do so much Lethal it wrapped around and did Aggravated damage in one shot, when my character was at full health beforehand. And that's something considered by other spirits to be on the scale of children or animals.<br /> <br /> Remember the Tenth Commandment: Celebrate the Awesome.<br /> <br /> Being a werewolf is fucking awesome. You can turn into a wolf, and howl, and kill things with your hands, and see the spirit world, and go toe-to-toe with monsters.<br /> <br /> Don't be ashamed to kick back and embrace the awesome sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-18-2016, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:03:01-07:00","id":989376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=989338#post989338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Urshul gave +2 to Strength, Willpower +3 to diceroll. Eating for flesh does Aggravated.<br /> <br /> I understand. If you're doing a mixed game you might tone it down, but really it's still a big cost for one action. Four Essence is a lot, and if they were to get the Tongue of Flame Gift they would be able to do it with a larger dicepool once they had the Purity for it. And that's without tying themselves to a lodge totem with a nasty ban.<br /> <br /> Werewolves face foes that are very powerful and can do a lot of damage very easily. The same character's first encounter with a Rank 2 spirit had the creature do so much Lethal it wrapped around and did Aggravated damage in one shot, when my character was at full health beforehand. And that's something considered by other spirits to be on the scale of children or animals.<br /> <br /> Remember the Tenth Commandment: Celebrate the Awesome.<br /> <br /> Being a werewolf is fucking awesome. You can turn into a wolf, and howl, and kill things with your hands, and see the spirit world, and go toe-to-toe with monsters.<br /> <br /> Don't be ashamed to kick back and embrace the awesome sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, awesome words my friend, I really dont know where it begins to feel strange, I plan t\u00f4 run next a mixed game and thats why a so careful with &quot;balance&quot; things, in my actual game I got five players, only two of them are veteran( alpha irraka storm lord 58 exp points and a rahu blood tallom with 52 exp), I think its better start to use some idigans, after all I plan finish the game by november.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T12:41:54-07:00","id":989490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=989320#post989320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that requires a rite. In first edition, at least, it was a four Dot Ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are known as rites in previous editions could be seen as extended action used to cause an Environmental Condition representing the portal to become Open in this edition (potentially at least), and thus totally (may) be appropriate to shortcut the process with appropriate Influence.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-18-2016, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T17:42:54-07:00","id":996352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=988738#post988738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood can clot internally. Have you never heard of deep vein thrombosis?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, but I am sure I don't want one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Running: <a href=\"https://shield-bearers.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Shield Bearers - W:TF 2nd</a><br /> Currently Planning: The Dead End Kids - CoD<br /> Untilted Tenra Bansho Zero game<br /> Currently Playing: <a href=\"http://theunusualsuspects.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Unusual Suspects - D:td</a>, I am playing <a href=\"http://www.noordinaryobsession.com/2016/08/19/unusual-suspects-naturalist/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naturalist</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","name":"salientmind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T03:47:38-07:00","id":997071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>salientmind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=996352#post996352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, but I am sure I don't want one.</div> </div> </div> </div>You definitely don't want one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T17:44:49-08:00","id":1000047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=988546#post988546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The persons blood would not clot in areas that lack damage, as the blood would not come in contact with collagen. So that isn't an issue either.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why you only use Create Death on part their body! Doesn't matter if the heart theoretically comes back alive, the rest of that person is unlikely to have survived its demise that long.<br /> Only half joking, it basically the only way Mage's direct damage spells inflicting lasting damage makes sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:53:48-08:00","id":1001076,"title":"","content":"Thanks s\u00f3 much for the thread, guys. I am running a story in S\u00e3o Paulo with me Players about the rise of a death spirit totem that wishes to compete with the city's ruling spirit, the Administrator, which is the ruler of the city spirit courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11882-bernagarou","name":"Bernagarou","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T11:37:09-08:00","id":1001411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bernagarou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=1001076#post1001076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks s\u00f3 much for the thread, guys. I am running a story in S\u00e3o Paulo with me Players about the rise of a death spirit totem that wishes to compete with the city's ruling spirit, the Administrator, which is the ruler of the city spirit courts.</div> </div> </div> </div>My money is on the City Spirit because the shaking of the status quo needed to replace a City Spirit with a Death Spirit would be fought by every single supernatural template, because you can be sure they wouldn't want the attention, loss of life, and financial collapse that kind of death would bring. Entire Forsaken, Kindred, Awakened, and Lost plot lines run counter to such potential upheavals.<br /> <br /> The city spirit practically represents the status quo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-10-2016, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T13:09:46-08:00","id":1001452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=1001411#post1001411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The city spirit practically represents the status quo.</div> </div> </div> </div>But a death spirit does represent the end of things.<br /> <br /> While there would be upheaval, it's not as if the place is in great straits in real life, without the addition of spirits vying over it. They've gotten past the drought, but didn't do anything to forestall another. And just as many supernaturals would be trying to make it go the other way, anyhow.<br /> <br /> It could go either way, which is what makes it a good plot point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-10-2016, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T13:36:36-08:00","id":1001465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987981-death-influence?p=1001452#post1001452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could go either way, which is what makes it a good plot point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree about it being an amazing regional tier plot, it being a major metropolitan area, it is like the Brazil equivalent to New York, New York but more developed and a stronger national economy to back it (the advantage of being an industrial nation as opposed to a post-industrial nation).<br /> <br /> And a death spirit defeating a city spirit sounds like what happened to Detroit or Flint; it is possible, but just so tragic. My money is still on the city spirit unless the chronicle is taking leap forwards in time, then the spread changes. The long game favors death and entropy after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-10-2016, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T15:02:40-08:00","id":1001511,"title":"","content":"You guys are thinking about this way more than I did. I just hoped to make a good story for a set of new players that aren\u00b4t experienced in the Forsaken game (even are not new to RPGs at all). I didn\u00b4t want to use Idigam at the start. In my story, the Death Spirit is a Totem to a large Pure pack and is using the pure to it\u00b4s own purposes as well. And it is &quot;seeding&quot; the city with circunstances that can create death ressonance (mass shootings, bad health care, and of course, CULTS! Because nothing is creepier than death cults). I try to make an arc of story on how each kind of prey is affected by it: So far, humans, a few vampires, and other spirits. The Administrator (think about the old guy in the room full of TVs in Matrix Reloaded) is starting to notice something is ... &quot;odd&quot;.<br /> <br /> I\u00b4m a foreigner to S\u00e3o Paulo, as I\u00b4ve just been living here for just three years, and I came from the northeast of the country, which has quite a different (and unique) make-up than the city I live in now. The Administor is my view of the essence ressonance of the city: Concrete, Alphalt, Information, Wealth and Blood of the people living in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11882-bernagarou","name":"Bernagarou","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T15:04:50-08:00","id":1001514,"title":"","content":"Anyway, thanks guys. You are giving me ideas. Please keep playing ball with me here on the forums, it\u00b4s my first experience with Forsaken 2nd edition. I tried to run a chronicle on the 1st but the game felt... wrong, weird. Maybe it was the Werewolf Apocalypse genetic storytelling detritus on me, the storyteller, but the game felt... limited. I like the new edition better on the width of stories you can tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11882-bernagarou","name":"Bernagarou","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}